class — Defines a structured data type with named fields.

Syntax:
  class MyClass {
    field1 string
    field2: int
    implements Printable {}
  }

Class fields can be written as `field Type` or `field: Type`. Fields can have default values, docstrings, attributes, methods, and `implements` blocks for interface contracts. Interface fields use the colon form.
